    <title>Street Science</title>
    <desc>Technically, Kevin Delaney is the director of visitor experience at Arkansas&apos; Museum of Discovery, but what he really does is create magic with science. When not wowing kids and inspiring adults with science experiments at the museum, Delaney hits the streets to perform stunts so unusual, offbeat, and unexpected, `mind-blowing&apos; comes to mind as an apt description. Hourlong episodes capture the magic as Kevin combines scientific knowledge with curiosity and old-fashioned ingenuity to produce fire, explosions and colourful reactions, and slow-motion replays provide viewers with extra insight. Featured experiments include creating a fire tornado, turning a leaf blower into a homemade hovercraft, and making an instant nitrogen cloud.</desc>
    <category>Series</category>
